Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["CanonicalStateForm", "ObjectName",
 CellID->983443855,ExpressionUUID->"9cf6e9f1-9b4b-8441-ba5d-853b3acf45b6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"f390e5b6-e090-cf42-9f12-31c5aaf1729d"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["CanonicalStateForm",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->
     "paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/\
CanonicalStateForm"], 
   RowBox[{"[", "state", "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9b0116e1-07dd-4541-a666-e3753274fbfa"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the canonical edge list of the hypergraph ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["state", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a9aeef85-c9d6-1f4a-acca-cc2ba4f6e2fe"],
 " in the active edge-symmetry universe (by default, unordered hyperedges \
with duplicates removed).",
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["CanonicalStateForm",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->
     "paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/\
CanonicalStateForm"], 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"state", ",", " ", "universe"}], "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"3d8db7e2-6f7a-3444-807b-6ad53da62937"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "uses the universe ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["universe", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "4eb90fde-d50d-2143-81cf-210b55cd4fb0"],
 ", either `\"Unordered\"` or `\"Ordered\"`.",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"8d1fc221-5feb-f544-add5-eef04e7bc060"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["CanonicalStateForm",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->
     "paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/\
CanonicalStateForm"], 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"state", ",", " ", "universe", ",", " ", "backend"}], "]"}]}]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"cd680364-2cb0-754a-ad5c-62358da9a2fe"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "uses the canonical-form backend ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["backend", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7531fd57-af6b-374a-b75a-d62139c528e8"],
 ", either `\"Exact\"` or `\"Native\"`.",
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["CanonicalStateForm",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->
     "paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/\
CanonicalStateForm"], 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"state", ",", " ", "\"\<Declared\>\"", ",", " ", "groups"}], 
    "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b3b9b9b7-6e61-874b-b38c-19781bd45657"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "treats hyperedges as ordered ports whose slot permutations in the per-arity \
groups ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["groups", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9f4d3da2-ec0b-364d-9165-a1cde2f21a6e"],
 " are symmetries."
}], "Usage",
 CellID->784306292,ExpressionUUID->"68c00252-a5a5-9146-91a7-73bd8cb61a2b"],

Cell["\<\
A hypergraph state is a list of hyperedges, each a list of vertices. The \
canonical form relabels vertices as 1, 2, ..., n and sorts the edge list.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->278402071,ExpressionUUID->"90ea10af-360a-b040-8866-e6ff22d5a2c8"],

Cell["\<\
Two states have the same canonical form exactly when they are isomorphic in \
the chosen universe: a vertex relabelling maps the edges of one onto the \
edges of the other, up to the slot symmetries of the universe.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->102305366,ExpressionUUID->"b299e0f1-0bcd-dd41-bbfc-ec3d32d7183a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the \"Unordered\" universe a hyperedge is an unordered set of slots and \
duplicate hyperedges are removed (simple hypergraphs). In the \"Ordered\" \
universe slot order and edge multiplicity are both semantic. In the \
\"Declared\" universe an edge of arity k stands for its orbit under the \
declared group for k, and multiplicity is semantic.",
 StyleBox["groups",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " is an Association arity -> group with groups \"Trivial\", \"Cyclic\", \
\"Dihedral\", \"Symmetric\", a permutation group object or a list of Cycles \
generators; the key \"Default\" applies to arities that are not listed."
}], "Notes",
 CellID->80792279,ExpressionUUID->"f7c6dde4-36a1-974a-8f48-467588fe90e6"],

Cell["\<\
The default backend \"Exact\" is an individualization-refinement canonical \
labelling. It is complete (equal forms exactly for isomorphic states) and \
invariant (independent of vertex names and edge order). It returns a Failure \
if its search exceeds an internal limit; only very symmetric states come near \
it.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->36007362,ExpressionUUID->"532b5be1-6132-9e44-b09b-dea9b91022de"],

Cell["\<\
The backend \"Native\" uses CanonicalHypergraph from the \
WolframInstitute/Hypergraph paclet. With Hypergraph 1.2.3 it is not invariant \
on some 3-ary states, so isomorphic copies can receive different forms. Every \
native form is still an isomorphic copy of its input, so native keys can only \
split isomorphism classes, never merge them.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->494174486,ExpressionUUID->"c066e565-2ac4-db4e-a01f-7c1d129e70be"],

